# Gaming Analytics & Player Behavior Dashboard

## Business Problem
The objective of this project is to analyse player engagement, churn risk, and revenue performance in a gaming environment. The goal is to identify key factors affecting player retention and optimise campaign spending for better ROI.

## Tools Used
- Power BI
- Python
- Excel

## Key Metrics Tracked
- Total Revenue
- Average Revenue per User (ARPU)
- Churn Risk
- Campaign Spend
- Users at Risk

## Analysis Performed
- Forecasted revenue trends to understand future performance
- Analysed churn distribution and identified at-risk users
- Compared churn across regions and age groups
- Evaluated campaign performance (CPA vs churn risk)
- Identified top-performing games by revenue
- Analysed user distribution across platforms

## Key Insights
- A small segment of users contributes significantly to total revenue
- Higher churn risk observed in specific user groups and regions
- Campaigns with high CPA and high churn risk require optimisation
- Peak engagement and revenue trends identified over time
- Platform distribution highlights key user segments for targeting

## Outcome
This dashboard enables:
- Identification of high-risk users for retention strategies
- Data-driven campaign optimisation decisions
- Improved understanding of revenue drivers and player behaviour
